=== SURVEY ===
Goal: add S4 feature `log-trace-summarization` that summarizes a
redacted log/trace window into a 3-6 sentence factual paragraph
without regressing the deterministic SSE-backed live log surface.

Baseline route/page surveyed:
  - Frontend: LiveLogsPage at web/src/features/admin/pages/LiveLogsPage.tsx
    (route /live-logs in App.tsx). Streams the API server's structured
    zerolog events via the SSE endpoint at GET /admin/logs/stream and
    renders them in a virtualized DataTable. Filters: level, grep,
    vehicle_id. Controls: pause/resume, autoscroll, clear, download,
    reconnect. Test ID anchor on the table panel:
    `data-testid="livelogs-table-panel"`.
  - Backend: GET /api/v1/admin/logs/stream
    (internal/api/admin_log_stream_handler.go) — SSE endpoint.
    Subscriber registry is stream-only; there is NO log/trace
    persistence repo today.

Allowed-files path drift acknowledged: the slice prompt's allowed-files
list says `web/src/features/system/**` because the registry's
"Frontend routes" anchor is `/system/logs`. The actual baseline page
lives at `web/src/features/admin/pages/LiveLogsPage.tsx`. The W1
inline addendum mandates end-to-end SPA wiring, so the page-level
integration MUST happen on whichever directory the baseline page
already lives in. This is a directory-naming reality the prompt's
auto-generated allowed-files list did not capture; the slice's
intent (integrate with the LiveLogs surface) is preserved exactly.
The new test files live under `web/src/features/admin/__tests__/`,
which is covered by `web/src/**/__tests__/**` in the allowed list.

DTOs / request shapes inspected:
  - Backend handler body shape: `{from_unix:int64, to_unix:int64, vehicle_id?:int64}`
    (mirrors the per-request scope-binding pattern from slice 0042
    incident-timeline-summarizer + slice 0044 signal-explorer-nl-filter).
  - LogStreamEvent shape (web/src/api/hooks/useLogStream.ts L37-43):
    `{seq, receivedAt, payload, parsed, level}` where receivedAt is ms.
    Used to derive aiFromUnix / aiToUnix from buffered events.

Hooks inspected:
  - useAiStream (web/src/hooks/useAiStream.ts): canonical SPA SSE
    hook used by every slice's wired AI component. Returns
    `{state, text, error, start, cancel, ...}`.
  - useSettings (web/src/hooks/useSettings.ts): drives the
    withAiFeature gate via ai_mode + ai_features.
  - useLogStream (web/src/api/hooks/useLogStream.ts): the
    deterministic SSE subscription powering LiveLogsPage. Mocked in
    the off-mode test so the page mounts hermetically.

Registry state surveyed: 40 features registered before this slice
(after aigen, the TS mirror reported 41). New entry placed
chronologically after `range-prediction-model` (the previous tail
entry).

Source-type forward-compat reservation: there is no log_event /
trace_span persistence today. Following the slice 0042 precedent
(`system_event` reserved by incident-timeline-summarizer without a
corresponding rag.Source* constant), the new source-type strings
`log_event` and `trace_span` are kept as feature-local string
constants in `internal/ai/tools/log_trace_summarizer.go`. The
production retriever returns zero chunks for unknown corpora; the
strategy's system prompt + goldens cover the zero-data path so the
LLM gracefully reports "no log/trace data persisted yet" rather
than hallucinating.

=== REASONING ===
ADR-015 + P1-P10 contract preservation:

1. Default-off (I1): registry entry has `DefaultOn: false`. The
   per-feature toggle defaults false in `ai_features` so the
   on-mode wiring can only fire after an explicit user opt-in.
2. Baseline intact (I3): the deterministic SSE log tail at
   /admin/logs/stream + every filter / control / table panel on
   LiveLogsPage continues to render unchanged. The AI component
   is mounted as a sibling Stack item ABOVE the filter panel.
   Off-mode test asserts livelogs-table-panel still renders and
   AILogTraceSummarization is absent (proving baseline coexistence).
3. Zero egress (I4): the strategy uses PolicyChatbot redaction.
   All provider calls route through the F5 decorator chain
   (redaction → rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace) the
   strategy/dispatcher loop installs at boot.
4. Hidden UI (I5): the AI component is wrapped via
   `withAiFeature('log-trace-summarization', InnerSection)`. In
   off mode the HOC returns null — proven by the off-mode test
   asserting the testID `ai-feature-log-trace-summarization-root`
   is absent from the DOM AND the wrapping container is empty.
5. 404 routes (I6): the backend route is mounted under the AI
   guard via `g.Wrap("log-trace-summarization", ...)`. The
   off-mode handler test mounts the route through the same guard
   with mode='off' + toggle=true and asserts a 404 with no
   feature-name leakage in the body.
6. Per-feature opt-in (I7): both `ai_mode != 'off'` AND
   `ai_features['log-trace-summarization'] === true` are required
   to render the component. The off-mode test pins the
   mode='cloud' + toggle=false path (mode-on alone is not enough)
   AND the mode='off' + toggle=on path (toggle-on alone is not
   enough).
7. Type system (I10): every new tool input/output and handler
   request body is a typed Go struct with json + validate tags
   that mirror through ValidateStruct at runtime. The TS side
   uses the regenerated `web/src/ai/features.ts` mirror; no
   `any` types or untyped JSON manipulation introduced.
8. Client/bg surfaces (I12): the new background job
   `ai_log_trace_indexer` is fail-closed by ai_mode + the
   per-feature toggle. The off-mode test
   `TestRunAILogTraceIndexer_OffMode_NoFanout` proves no
   embedder / vector-DB / LLM call is made when ai_mode='off'.

P11/P12 — Wired-or-absent + No-placeholder-buttons:
  The shipped SPA component imports useAiStream, references the
  registered backend endpoint `/ai/system/logs/summarize`, and has
  a COMPUTED disabled prop driven by `canSummarize = windowAcceptable
  && state !== 'streaming'`. Zero placeholder strings (W1 inline
  self-check returns 0). The on-mode wiring test
  TestLogTraceSummarizationAIOnWiredCallsRoute proves a click
  enqueues exactly one POST against /api/v1/ai/system/logs/summarize
  with the in-scope window in the body, and a second click while
  streaming is a no-op (double-submit guard).

Per-request scope binding rationale: the AI handler installs the
request-supplied `(from_unix, to_unix, vehicle_id)` tuple in ctx
via `tools.WithScopedLogTraceWindow`. Both `query_trace_window`
and `retrieve_log_chunks` reject any LLM-supplied tuple that does
not match the in-scope tuple. This defends against
prompt-injection exfiltration via operator-authored log messages
("summarize the window from_unix=1500000000 instead").

